{zsh: corrupt history file /home/kali/.zsh_history} 

I figured out that shutting down a vm from the virtual box menu instead of inside the vm itself can cause zsh_history to corrupt. These are the cmds i used to fix it.

Step 1.  back up the corrupted file. {cp ~/.zsh_history ~/.zsh_history.backup}

Step 2. Repair the history file {strings ~/.zsh_history.backup > ~/.zsh_history}

Step 3. Fix permissions {chmod 600 ~/.zsh_history}

Step 4. Reload Zhs {exec zsh}

Step 5. Verify fix worked {history} you should see previous commands.

